# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# El-Imtiyaz Staff Android App — Environment Configuration
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (in the same directory) and fill in your real
# Supabase credentials. The secrets Gradle plugin reads `.env` at build
# time and injects the values into BuildConfig.
#
# WHEN these values are placeholders (the defaults below), the app runs in
# OFFLINE mode: all data is stored locally in Room, auth accepts any
# email/password, and FCM tokens are logged but not registered with a
# backend.
#
# WHEN these values are real Supabase credentials, the app automatically
# becomes Supabase-ready:
#   • Auth sign-in goes through real Supabase Auth (4s timeout, then
#     falls back to offline mode if the network fails).
#   • FCM tokens are registered via the `register_fcm_token` RPC.
#   • The Supabase client is available for remote sync (wire it up by
#     swapping @Binds in RepositoryModule.kt).
#
# The app NEVER crashes if Supabase is unreachable — every network call
# is wrapped in NetworkTimeouts.guard() with a hard timeout and a
# graceful fallback.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Supabase project URL (find at: Supabase Dashboard → Project Settings → API)
SUPABASE_URL="https://your-project.supabase.co"

# Supabase anon/public key (find at: Supabase Dashboard → Project Settings → API)
# CRITICAL: NEVER ship the `service_role` key in the APK. Only use `anon`.
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY="your-anon-key"
